jobs.description:
Robert Half is currently recruiting a Financial Controller (m/f/x)

Our client is an international organization active in a fast-moving distribution and supply chain environment.

The scope of responsibilities for this job as a Financial Controller (m/f/x) include:

• you ensure the accuracy of accounting, reporting, and compliance in close collaboration with local accounting and international finance teams;
• you act as a right hand to the Finance Manager and support local management with reporting, ad hoc analysis, and financial insights;
• you perform monthly internal audit activities, including control follow-up and cycle count support;
• you support quarterly and annual external audits and provide requested data to auditors and relevant stakeholders;
• you assist with tax, customs, and compliance-related audits and documentation;
• you prepare and monitor financial reporting, including balance sheet and P&L follow-up;
• you contribute to monthly KPI, cash flow, working capital, and forecasting analysis;
• you coordinate transfer pricing documentation and support statutory and group reporting requirements;
• you review ageing reports and follow up on key financial indicators;
• you assist in the annual budget process, rolling forecasts, and variance analysis;
• you support monthly, quarterly, and yearly closing activities and help the team meet strict deadlines;
• you identify process improvement opportunities, maintain procedures, and contribute to finance-related projects such as e-invoicing, ERP enhancements, treasury tools, and reporting solutions.

The requested qualifications for this job include:

• you hold a master's degree in Finance, Business, or a related field;
• you have at least 5 years of experience in audit and/or controlling within an international environment;
• you have a strong knowledge of Belgian GAAP and IFRS;
• you bring solid analytical skills and know how to translate figures into meaningful business insights;
• you are comfortable working in a structured, detail-oriented, and deadline-driven way;
• you communicate confidently with stakeholders across finance, sales, operations, and support functions;
• you are proactive, hands-on, and able to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment;
• you are a team player with a collaborative mindset and a strong sense of ownership;
• you have advanced Excel skills, good ERP knowledge, and ideally experience with SAP and Power BI;
• you have an excellent command of English and preferably also speak Dutch.
